 "hypothesis": "H38-1: on a fixed detector surface, buying dots by exact incremental triangular-kernel credit per unit false-positive mass (plug-in truth density proportional to the surface, break-even stopping at alpha*D/(1-alpha*D)) raises credit per emitted pixel versus fixed-spacing score-ordered dotting, because the metric pays only for the maximum kernel over nearby dots and fixed budgets force-spend FP mass in barren terrain while under-covering short high-credit segments.",
 "mechanism": "DTI = TP/(0.2(TP+FP)+0.8N); detector (H35 arm B) and candidate pool (ridge-NMS top 3.5%) are identical across arms, so only the selection rule changes. Greedy maximises dTP_hat/dFP_hat with dTP_hat = sum_g phat_g*max(0,k-cur_g) (exact max-kernel incremental accounting, submodular) and dFP_hat = 1-E[max_g k*Bern(phat_g)] under neighbour independence; phat is the surface normalised to Nhat = 0.25*|visible catalogue in domain|.",
 "non_fault_process_that_could_mimic_it": "No new geology: the lane inherits the H35 detector's mimics (lithologic/intrusive contacts, basin-margin pinch-outs). Lane-specific failure mode: phat is the detector's own uncalibrated score, so greedy spending amplifies the detector's systematic errors, and the independence approximation understates FP along continuous false lineaments (roads, flight-line levelling, fan-lobe edges).",
